WEBVTT

01:00.390 --> 01:07.230
It is said that 70% of the
human brain's capacity is unused.

01:09.230 --> 01:11.290
It's also thought that...

01:11.870 --> 01:15.060
...the mysterious powers that humans
have are hidden in this part of the brain.

01:17.010 --> 01:21.570
The 70% of the brain that is not used...

01:22.340 --> 01:24.070
...is often called this...

01:24.150 --> 01:37.390
<i>Night Head Genesis</i>

01:37.390 --> 01:41.450
Good evening,
great teacher Tsukasa Kamiya.

01:41.960 --> 01:43.900
Here, open wide.

01:47.540 --> 01:51.630
Kamiya, your job is already done.

02:05.350 --> 02:06.460
<i>Bewilderment</i>

02:06.460 --> 02:10.290
<i>Bewilderment
Episode 12</i>

02:15.360 --> 02:18.160
There was a time I flew in the air.

02:22.740 --> 02:27.770
It was one day after being locked up
in the research lab for three years.

03:21.500 --> 03:24.400
I know! Why don't I go back
to the house like this!

03:52.930 --> 03:55.730
Damn it, let me out! Let me out!

03:56.970 --> 03:58.960
The one that made the wall...

03:59.200 --> 04:02.970
...was predicting that one day
I was going to fly in the sky too?

04:10.280 --> 04:11.680
Brother!

04:14.580 --> 04:16.380
Hey, Brother!

04:16.850 --> 04:17.940
Brother!

04:19.460 --> 04:20.790
Wake up!

04:22.760 --> 04:23.850
Brother!

04:31.100 --> 04:32.330
Thank goodness...

05:00.860 --> 05:01.630
Brother.

05:03.470 --> 05:04.560
It's from Mr. Mikuriya.

05:10.010 --> 05:12.030
A note by Tsukasa Kamiya, huh?

05:14.280 --> 05:16.710
"Predictions regarding Naoto Kirihara"?

05:17.780 --> 05:19.750
"Too enormous of a power."

05:20.180 --> 05:23.020
"Division. Two bodies."

05:23.990 --> 05:26.550
"Beasts that feast on the flesh."

05:26.990 --> 05:29.720
"Separation will lead to
madness and death."

05:30.960 --> 05:35.120
"There is no forward to darkness,
but reformation is white."

05:36.070 --> 05:38.030
What is this?

05:39.200 --> 05:40.860
What is he trying to say?

05:43.940 --> 05:46.770
"Separation will lead to
madness and death."

05:46.980 --> 05:48.910
Is this pointing to you and me?

05:49.450 --> 05:52.110
"Beasts that feast on the flesh."

05:53.320 --> 05:56.550
Does that mean there are those
we are going to fight against?

05:56.620 --> 05:57.920
Beasts?

05:58.290 --> 06:01.050
Does that mean the opponent
isn't just one person?

06:01.860 --> 06:04.720
What do they mean by
"reformation is white"?

06:05.290 --> 06:09.160
Meaning mankind avoiding
its destruction with the virus...

06:09.230 --> 06:11.890
...wasn't the reformation?

06:12.670 --> 06:18.700
Brother, when I heard reformation
the first time, I was really scared.

06:19.880 --> 06:23.040
I had a feeling it was
something that was huge.

06:24.450 --> 06:28.540
But if something is to
happen from here on...

06:28.620 --> 06:32.680
...I don't think we should
avoid it and go on.

06:37.130 --> 06:42.190
You two are existences
that are definitely needed for...

06:42.260 --> 06:45.170
...the big reformation
that is coming later.

06:59.210 --> 07:02.240
"Beasts that feast on the flesh."

07:02.820 --> 07:08.690
Naoya, maybe that barrier
was protecting us.

07:13.000 --> 07:13.980
Brother...

07:14.760 --> 07:17.530
There is no barrier anymore, right?

07:18.230 --> 07:19.130
Yeah.

07:28.610 --> 07:33.310
The number that you have
dialed is definitely on a tie-up.

07:33.550 --> 07:36.880
We are in the middle of looking into it,
but because it is in such a...

07:36.950 --> 07:39.220
...depopulated area,
we will need more time.

07:42.690 --> 07:44.780
Maybe something
actually did happen.

07:45.230 --> 07:46.350
Yeah, you're right.

07:46.500 --> 07:47.760
We should go back.

07:48.830 --> 07:50.660
Hey, you guys.

07:53.470 --> 07:57.170
I would like to talk to you for a little.
Is that okay?

07:57.710 --> 07:58.570
Well...

07:58.640 --> 07:59.770
We're in a hurry.

08:01.610 --> 08:03.700
Hey! Wait up!

08:03.780 --> 08:04.680
Hey!

08:05.150 --> 08:07.010
Come on, you're so cold.

08:07.080 --> 08:10.110
So, hey, it's a really good offer.

08:10.750 --> 08:14.420
The truth is I'm this kind of person.

08:14.490 --> 08:16.360
<i>Purple Chain Entertainment
Youko Namekawa</i>

08:17.160 --> 08:18.350
Purple Chain?

08:20.160 --> 08:21.690
You don't know?

08:21.760 --> 08:25.030
Clubs and famous restaurants...

08:25.100 --> 08:28.400
We are featured in magazines
and the like a lot.

08:28.570 --> 08:30.600
We're also a
talent management company!

08:30.670 --> 08:33.730
Well this is really the main part, but...

08:34.440 --> 08:35.970
I know! I know!

08:36.110 --> 08:39.170
You guys came from
the countryside just now, right?

08:39.250 --> 08:42.380
You're lucky having me
be the first one to talk to you.

08:42.450 --> 08:45.750
There are a lot of
different bad ones in Tokyo.

08:45.820 --> 08:48.480
Seeing that you're wandering around
in the middle of a work day...

08:48.560 --> 08:51.580
...you're not working at
a good job or anything, right?

08:51.730 --> 08:55.820
Don't you want to make a lot of money
and have a luxurious living?

08:55.900 --> 08:58.630
Flat out, monthly salary,
2 million yen!

08:58.700 --> 09:00.220
Hey, won't you come with me?

09:00.300 --> 09:03.030
I really want to talk
to you about it in detail!

09:03.970 --> 09:04.730
Let's go, Naoya.

09:04.810 --> 09:06.000
Hey!

09:06.070 --> 09:08.410
If you give me that kind of attitude,
you're going to miss out!

09:08.480 --> 09:11.170
This is such a big chance!

09:11.380 --> 09:12.570
Hey!

09:12.680 --> 09:14.270
Hold on!

09:14.450 --> 09:18.250
If you sign the contract with us,
we'll make sure your future is bright!

09:18.320 --> 09:20.220
Wow, you have long legs!

09:20.290 --> 09:22.190
Half? Or are you a quarter?

09:22.260 --> 09:23.050
Leave us alone!

09:23.130 --> 09:24.090
Hey, wait!

09:29.870 --> 09:30.960
We're sorry.

09:36.670 --> 09:37.760
What!

09:37.840 --> 09:41.710
Just because you guys are a little handsome,
you think you can do anything?

09:41.780 --> 09:43.140
You'll regret it!

09:43.210 --> 09:45.310
You will definitely regret it!

09:47.980 --> 09:48.920
Were you okay?

09:50.190 --> 09:51.680
I found out that...

09:51.750 --> 09:55.780
...as long as I have my heart prepared,
I won't see much that will shock me.

09:56.230 --> 09:57.390
Is that so?

10:04.770 --> 10:06.670
Today is a bad biorhythm day.

10:08.740 --> 10:12.000
We're unconsciously
letting out a bad surge.

10:12.470 --> 10:15.030
That's why a woman
like her comes near us.

10:15.110 --> 10:18.670
But thanks to that, I was able to
realize that I have been growing.

10:20.080 --> 10:21.140
That's true.

10:24.690 --> 10:26.550
Please call the police! Hurry!

10:27.090 --> 10:28.320
What's the matter?

10:28.420 --> 10:30.480
There's a person
on the roof across the street!

10:30.560 --> 10:33.690
It seems like she's going to jump!
A woman! Hurry!

10:34.100 --> 10:35.090
Brother...

10:58.520 --> 11:01.010
Brother, it's that woman!

11:06.030 --> 11:07.120
Why?

11:27.580 --> 11:28.340
Don't!

11:45.970 --> 11:47.960
Hey, where is the ambulance!

12:02.320 --> 12:06.480
From up there,
the woman just came down and...

12:10.960 --> 12:12.590
Brother, over there!

12:19.070 --> 12:20.560
M-Masayuki?

12:27.710 --> 12:28.700
Toru?

12:29.640 --> 12:31.670
It's there in the back room.

12:34.150 --> 12:36.580
Let us see the person
that's in the back over there.

12:36.650 --> 12:37.580
What?

12:37.850 --> 12:39.510
What's up with you guys?

12:45.630 --> 12:49.390
Those guys killed my dog.

12:52.100 --> 12:53.590
He was my friend.

12:54.640 --> 12:56.070
I loved him.

12:57.870 --> 12:58.970
Those guys...

13:00.110 --> 13:01.700
Let's contact Mikuriya.

13:03.710 --> 13:05.700
What? What are you going to do?

13:06.110 --> 13:09.850
I think it's best for him to be put
in custody of a guy named Mikuriya.

13:09.920 --> 13:12.250
Put in custody?
What do you mean by "put in custody"!

13:12.320 --> 13:13.980
I won't let him go anywhere!

13:14.060 --> 13:16.750
I won't... I won't let
something like that happen!

13:17.830 --> 13:20.920
Are you fine with
letting this boy kill more people?

13:21.530 --> 13:22.590
It can't be...

13:22.830 --> 13:23.760
No...

13:23.830 --> 13:24.860
That can't be...

13:29.540 --> 13:30.530
Why?

13:30.740 --> 13:32.300
Why are you in a place like this?

13:32.370 --> 13:35.470
Mr. Mikuriya said I could leave already.

13:35.810 --> 13:37.570
Mr. Mikuriya said that?

13:38.580 --> 13:41.050
Then is the research lab okay?

13:41.420 --> 13:42.440
I don't know.

13:42.650 --> 13:44.480
What do you mean by "I don't know"?

13:44.550 --> 13:47.450
Because we left already.

13:47.720 --> 13:49.020
Where's your mom?

13:49.460 --> 13:51.150
She's shopping over there.

13:54.130 --> 13:57.570
The woman that fell before...
She's a bad person, right?

13:58.970 --> 14:00.060
What?

14:00.370 --> 14:04.300
Masayuki, what did you learn
at the research lab?

14:04.710 --> 14:06.670
Mr. Mikuriya is wrong.

14:06.940 --> 14:07.810
What?

14:07.980 --> 14:12.310
We are much more important
than normal people.

14:12.450 --> 14:13.610
Important?

14:14.050 --> 14:15.020
Yeah.

14:15.450 --> 14:22.550
Well, we need to use our powers
to get rid of those bad people.

14:22.920 --> 14:24.360
You don't mean you did...

14:24.430 --> 14:26.620
The power is there to be used.

14:27.160 --> 14:29.530
I think it's wrong to hold it in.

14:30.630 --> 14:31.720
Wait, Masayuki!

14:47.720 --> 14:49.080
Damn it, where is he?

14:49.920 --> 14:52.320
Masayuki is worse than before.

14:54.090 --> 14:55.390
What is going on?

15:14.440 --> 15:15.670
He's quick!

15:22.650 --> 15:25.050
Then for that,
this curtain color would be better.

15:41.870 --> 15:44.460
Oh, you guys are...

15:45.110 --> 15:46.540
Where is Masayuki?

15:49.210 --> 15:53.040
I don't know.
He was around here until a while ago.

15:53.450 --> 15:55.280
He is hiding somewhere.

15:55.680 --> 15:58.810
Why does Masayuki
have to hide somewhere?

16:00.390 --> 16:01.180
Masayuki!

16:09.630 --> 16:10.790
Sir...

16:13.370 --> 16:15.230
Is there something wrong?

16:16.640 --> 16:17.940
What's wrong?

16:18.210 --> 16:19.500
Brother Naoto...

16:24.550 --> 16:25.480
Hey...

16:25.810 --> 16:27.080
What's wrong?

16:28.580 --> 16:29.810
What is this?

16:49.170 --> 16:50.160
Damn it.

16:50.510 --> 16:51.670
What's with you guys!

16:52.740 --> 16:54.300
Brother, it's different!

16:54.610 --> 16:55.910
It's different from that time!

17:00.720 --> 17:02.770
Just who are...

17:03.790 --> 17:04.580
Who are these guys!

17:05.120 --> 17:06.680
No, Brother!

17:21.940 --> 17:23.670
It's different, Brother.

17:23.940 --> 17:25.060
That just now...

17:25.140 --> 17:27.010
That just now didn't have an entity.

17:27.080 --> 17:28.130
What!

17:28.210 --> 17:30.700
You believe what Mikuriya says.

17:30.780 --> 17:32.640
That's why something
like that comes out.

17:32.710 --> 17:33.700
What?

17:33.850 --> 17:36.940
It's because you guys have a
hesitancy with the powers you have.

17:37.020 --> 17:39.280
That's why a monster
like that is born.

17:39.420 --> 17:43.410
Those are the materialized forms
of the negative consciousness that...

17:43.490 --> 17:46.360
...you have been holding
deep down within your hearts.

17:47.160 --> 17:50.290
That man pulled us closer.

17:51.200 --> 17:53.130
That man... to Miki...

18:08.820 --> 18:12.780
Man, you haven't been
comprehending anything, have you?

18:13.120 --> 18:13.990
What?

18:18.360 --> 18:20.880
You guys have strong power.

18:20.960 --> 18:25.590
And that power is big enough
to change the real world.

18:25.700 --> 18:26.670
That's why...

18:27.900 --> 18:28.960
What...

18:29.170 --> 18:31.260
Our negative consciousness?

18:31.340 --> 18:34.710
The feeling of not wanting to know
the reason for existence...

18:34.780 --> 18:37.140
...turned into intent to kill toward Miki.

18:37.250 --> 18:40.340
The feeling of wanting to turn
your back on the truth gave birth to...

18:40.420 --> 18:45.150
...a consciousness feeling the need
to kill those who try to speak the truth.

18:49.660 --> 18:52.420
The ones that created
those men are us?

18:52.490 --> 18:54.220
Something like that can't...

18:55.300 --> 18:56.090
Masayuki?

19:13.480 --> 19:14.540
Mr. Naoya...

19:26.260 --> 19:29.390
Mr. Naoya, I'm not saying it.

19:30.670 --> 19:32.030
It's not me.

19:32.100 --> 19:33.930
It's a scary man.

19:34.700 --> 19:35.730
Masayuki!

19:38.670 --> 19:41.160
This is mind control!

19:41.280 --> 19:42.040
Yeah...

19:45.210 --> 19:47.180
Please get it together!

19:47.480 --> 19:49.010
Are you okay?

19:49.880 --> 19:50.820
Who is it!

19:50.950 --> 19:51.980
Where are you!

19:53.050 --> 19:54.020
Show yourself!

19:56.060 --> 19:56.850
Brother!

20:28.820 --> 20:31.550
What do you think I am?

20:32.490 --> 20:37.160
Naoto, did you think about me
even for a little when you were leaving?

20:37.870 --> 20:39.360
Well? Naoto?

20:44.510 --> 20:45.700
You guys...

20:46.670 --> 20:50.940
Thanks to you guys,
my life was totally messed up!

20:51.010 --> 20:55.640
If you guys hadn't come,
we would have kept on getting along fine!

20:55.880 --> 20:59.080
The ones that shattered
my life were you guys!

20:59.290 --> 21:00.310
It's you guys!

21:09.930 --> 21:13.200
We just wanted normal children.

21:13.470 --> 21:16.270
We didn't need children like you guys.

21:16.440 --> 21:17.300
It's you guys!

21:33.090 --> 21:33.820
Naoya!

21:43.200 --> 21:44.100
Brother!

21:44.270 --> 21:46.560
Someone is going
through our memories!

22:07.160 --> 22:08.750
Damn it. Where is he?

22:15.000 --> 22:15.860
Brother!

22:16.230 --> 22:17.130
Outside!

22:17.230 --> 22:18.560
He's most likely outside!

22:29.910 --> 22:38.720
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:47.560
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

22:47.630 --> 22:56.400
<i>A single shadow looked like light
in this world that I'm imprisoned in.</i>

22:56.470 --> 23:05.210
<i>The rain of May became lighter
as it was kindly shining tomorrow.</i>

23:05.280 --> 23:09.610
<i>I lost the meaning of smiling...</i>

23:09.680 --> 23:13.980
<i>... that day I thought I
lost my place to be.</i>

23:14.060 --> 23:18.420
<i>I wished for your warmth.</i>

23:18.490 --> 23:22.930
<i>We have stopped time.</i>

23:23.160 --> 23:27.260
<i>I had this feeling it was
eventually going to come, but...</i>

23:27.340 --> 23:31.900
<i>... I pretended I didn't know
and buried my loneliness.</i>

23:31.970 --> 23:42.080
<i>I looked down at your feet as the
droplets describing "Good-bye" fell.</i>

23:42.720 --> 23:51.460
<i>I hope that everything that
makes you sad will all disappear.</i>

23:51.530 --> 23:59.900
<i>The words that I said that day
are still tightening my chest.</i>

24:01.770 --> 24:04.140
Arrogance called "the chosen ones."

24:04.770 --> 24:07.430
Deception called
"liberalization of instinct."

24:08.280 --> 24:10.800
The consciousness
of a great someone that...

24:10.880 --> 24:13.940
...hides itself and shows itself
within the poppy of darkness.

24:14.150 --> 24:18.640
When the anger that was compressed
to its limit hits its critical point...

24:19.120 --> 24:22.650
...the potentiality of a
wondrous power starts a rampage.

24:23.390 --> 24:29.860
<i>Episode 13, "Game"</i>

24:26.090 --> 24:29.200
Where are we headed?
